40117966 Preserve the Xorg keyboard layout when no input source is available

Solaris does not provide systemd-localed.  Xorg configures the system keyboard
using HAL or xorg.conf; deriving a replacement from the UI locale can select
an unrelated layout (ja_JP maps to the unavailable IBus engine anthy).

Leave Xorg's keymap unchanged when the greeter or user session has no usable
input source.  Explicitly configured, available sources continue to be applied.
Do not select a replacement IBus engine either: an XKB echo engine can also
reset the Xorg layout. Handle an absent source in the indicator and on-screen
keyboard as well.

Solaris integration: not suitable for upstream in this form.

--- a/js/ui/status/keyboard.js
+++ b/js/ui/status/keyboard.js
@@ -591,12 +591,8 @@
                 infosList.push({type, id, displayName, shortName});
         }
 
-        if (infosList.length === 0) {
-            let type = INPUT_SOURCE_TYPE_XKB;
-            let id = KeyboardManager.DEFAULT_LAYOUT;
-            let [, displayName, shortName] = this._xkbInfo.get_layout_info(id);
-            infosList.push({type, id, displayName, shortName});
-        }
+        // With no usable input source, retain Xorg's configured keymap.
+        // An unavailable IBus engine must not force a US keyboard layout.
 
         let inputSourcesByShortName = {};
         for (let i = 0; i < infosList.length; i++) {
@@ -631,6 +627,8 @@
 
